\image(figures/krr_linear_weights.svg)
// result_end
\caption(A linear kernel matches primal ridge, and the fitted line extrapolates beyond the response range.)
\alttext(At x equals three, the fitted value is 3.5 from response weights minus 0.75 and 1.75. One weight becomes negative outside the anchors while their sum stays one.)

>> Four rows: which leave-one-out question are we asking?

Use \(x=(0,1,2,10)\), \(y=(0,1,0,2)\), RBF gamma one and lambda 0.1.
Full-data mean and population SD of x are 3.25 and about 3.961. Deleting x=10
changes them to one and \(\sqrt{2/3}\). This changes relative distances and hence
the kernel even though gamma stays numerically fixed. The fast fixed-metric LOO
MSE is about 1.9112; four genuine preprocessing refits give about 1.5837. Neither
quantity is a universal upper or lower bound on the other. The right panel records
what each deleted fit actually learned.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/krr_preprocessing.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2, 10});
  d.add_column("y", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 0, 2});
  dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions o;
  o.lambda = .1;
  o.gamma  = 1;
  const dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegression m(d, "y ~ x", o);
  const auto cv   = dm::stats::kernel_ridge_cross_validate(d, "y ~ x", {o}, {0, 1, 2, 3});
  const auto pred = cv.predictions.sort_by("row");
  const auto rows = pred.numeric_column("row").values();
  auto       p =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .points(rows, pred.numeric_column("observed").values(), "observed", {30, 30, 30}, 4)
          .line(rows, m.fitted_values(), "fixed metric", {40, 100, 190})
          .line(rows, pred.numeric_column("prediction").values(), "refit metric", {190, 100, 35})
          .title("Two deletion procedures")
          .x_label("deleted row")
          .y_label("response / prediction")
          .x_limits(-.1, 3.1)
          .y_limits(-.6, 3.3)
          .legend(
              {"observed", "fixed metric", "refit metric"},
              {{30, 30, 30}, {40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}});
  auto scales =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .line(rows, cv.folds.numeric_column("mean_0").values(), "fold mean", {40, 100, 190})
          .line(rows, cv.folds.numeric_column("scale_0").values(), "fold SD", {190, 100, 35})
          .title("Training-only x preprocessing")
          .x_label("deleted row")
          .y_label("raw x units")
          .x_limits(-.1, 3.1)
          .y_limits(0, 6.5)
          .legend({"fold mean", "fold SD"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}});
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(p).add(scales).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/krr_preprocessing.svg");
  std::print(
      "Full metric: mean={:.6f}, population SD={:.6f}; fixed-metric LOO "
      "MSE={:.6f}.\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n",
      m.feature_mean()[0],
      m.feature_scale()[0],
      m.rmse() * m.rmse(),
      cv.candidates.to_md(6),
      cv.folds.to_md(6),
      pred.to_md(6));
}
```
