\caption(The fixed-kernel penalty path obeys the spectral complexity and optimality inequalities.)
\alttext(Effective degrees of freedom decrease with lambda. Training RMSE rises, while fixed-metric LOO and known-mean errors reflect both smoothing bias and sampling noise.)

> A dataset example: Iris petal regression

>> Declare the holdout and tune within the remaining rows

`dm::datasets::iris()` contains 150 flowers, 50 per species, with four numeric
measurements in centimetres and a species label. Predict `Petal.Length` from
`Petal.Width`; this is regression of measurements, not species classification.
The pooled relation partly reflects differences between species. We leave out
original rows 0, 5, 10, ... for final evaluation: 30 flowers, ten per species.
The remaining 120 rows supply all tuning and preprocessing. This deterministic
split is transparent, but does not quantify population uncertainty or robustness
to a different sampling scheme.

Inside those 120 rows, fold ID is retained-row index modulo four. Every validation
fold has 30 rows (ten per species) and 90 fitting rows. Compare RBF gammas
0.1, one and ten, each at lambda 0.01, 0.1 and one, plus the linear kernel at
those three penalties. Each of the 48 fold fits learns its own scaling. Gamma
values are therefore comparable in training-standardised units, without importing
validation-row SDs. We choose the first minimum pooled validation MSE, then refit
that fixed candidate on all 120 fitting rows. The 30 holdout rows take no part in
this choice. Fold means and SDs below belong to the winning candidate only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/krr_iris_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto               iris = dm::datasets::iris();
  std::vector<std::size_t> rows;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < iris.nrows(); ++i)
    if (i % 5 != 0)
      rows.push_back(i);
  const auto train   = iris.take_rows(rows);
  const auto summary = train | dm::group_by("Species") |
                       dm::summarise(
                           dm::agg::n("n"),
                           dm::agg::mean("Petal.Length", "mean_length_cm"),
                           dm::agg::mean("Petal.Width", "mean_width_cm"));
  std::vector<std::size_t> folds(train.nrows());
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < folds.size(); ++i)
    folds[i] = i % 4;
  std::vector<dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions> candidates;
  for (double g : {.1, 1., 10.})
    for (double l : {.01, .1, 1.}) {
      dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions o;
      o.gamma  = g;
      o.lambda = l;
      candidates.push_back(o);
    }
  for (double l : {.01, .1, 1.}) {
    dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions o;
    o.kernel = "linear";
    o.lambda = l;
    candidates.push_back(o);
  }
  const auto cv = dm::stats::kernel_ridge_cross_validate(
      train, "Petal.Length ~ Petal.Width", candidates, folds);
  const std::vector<std::string>       labels{"RBF 0.1", "RBF 1", "RBF 10", "linear"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{
      {40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}, {70, 145, 90}, {130, 85, 155}};
  auto curve = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (std::size_t group = 0; group < 4; ++group) {
    std::vector<double> error;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
      error.push_back(cv.candidates.double_at("rmse", 3 * group + i));
    curve.line({-2, -1, 0}, error, labels[group], colors[group]);
  }
  curve.title("Four-fold tuning on 120 flowers")
      .x_label("log10 lambda")
      .y_label("pooled validation RMSE (cm)")
      .x_limits(-2, 0)
      .y_limits(.2, .9)
      .legend(labels, colors);
  const auto local = cv.folds.filter(
      [&](const auto& r) { return r.get_double("candidate") == double(cv.best_candidate); });
  auto metric = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                    .line(
                        local.numeric_column("fold").values(),
                        local.numeric_column("mean_0").values(),
                        "training mean",
                        colors[0])
                    .line(
                        local.numeric_column("fold").values(),
                        local.numeric_column("scale_0").values(),
                        "training SD",
                        colors[1])
                    .title("Winning candidate: fold metrics")
                    .x_label("validation fold")
                    .y_label("petal width (cm)")
                    .x_limits(0, 3)
                    .y_limits(0, 2)
                    .legend({"training mean", "training SD"}, {colors[0], colors[1]});
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(curve).add(metric).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/krr_iris_validation.svg");
  std::print(
      "Dataset: {} rows; fitting: {}; untouched holdout: 30.\n\nTraining-only "
      "summaries\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n",
      iris.nrows(),
      train.nrows(),
      summary.to_md(6),
      cv.candidates.to_md(6),
      local.to_md(6));
}
```
