\alttext(Four curves compare pooled validation RMSE across three penalties. The second panel shows the winning candidate training mean and population SD in each of four folds.)

>> Refit the chosen model and evaluate the untouched rows

The following complete program repeats the declared tuning protocol, refits its
winner once, and scores all 30 held-out flowers. The baseline always predicts
the **120-row training response mean**. R-squared uses variation about the
holdout response mean, so its baseline differs from that reported baseline RMSE.
The training and fixed-metric LOO diagnostics printed alongside it describe the
refitted model; they are not substituted for held-out performance.
On this split, RBF gamma 0.1 and lambda 0.01 win with pooled validation RMSE
0.402698 cm. The refitted df is 3.9336. Held-out RMSE is 0.366721 cm versus
1.816220 cm for the training-mean predictor, with held-out R-squared 0.959029.
The holdout result happens to be better than the tuning score; this ordering is
not guaranteed by the procedure.
No confidence band is shown because this estimator does not supply predictive
uncertainty. The fitted curve covers only the observed petal-width range.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/krr_iris_holdout.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto               iris = dm::datasets::iris();
  std::vector<std::size_t> a, b;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < iris.nrows(); ++i)
    (i % 5 == 0 ? b : a).push_back(i);
  const auto               train = iris.take_rows(a), test = iris.take_rows(b);
  std::vector<std::size_t> folds(train.nrows());
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < folds.size(); ++i)
    folds[i] = i % 4;
  std::vector<dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions> candidates;
  for (double g : {.1, 1., 10.})
    for (double l : {.01, .1, 1.}) {
      dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions o;
      o.gamma  = g;
      o.lambda = l;
      candidates.push_back(o);
    }
  for (double l : {.01, .1, 1.}) {
    dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegressionOptions o;
    o.kernel = "linear";
    o.lambda = l;
    candidates.push_back(o);
  }
  const auto cv = dm::stats::kernel_ridge_cross_validate(
      train, "Petal.Length ~ Petal.Width", candidates, folds);
  const dm::stats::KernelRidgeRegression m(
      train, "Petal.Length ~ Petal.Width", candidates[cv.best_candidate]);
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame q;
  q.add_column("Petal.Width", dm::seql(.1, 2.5, 201).values());
  const auto pred = m.predict(test);
  auto       fit  = dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
                 .points(
                     train.numeric_column("Petal.Width").values(),
                     train.numeric_column("Petal.Length").values(),
                     "training",
                     {150, 150, 150},
                     2)
                 .points(
                     test.numeric_column("Petal.Width").values(),
                     test.numeric_column("Petal.Length").values(),
                     "holdout",
                     {190, 100, 35},
                     3)
                 .line(
                     q.numeric_column("Petal.Width").values(),
                     m.predict(q),
                     "selected fit",
                     {40, 100, 190})
                 .title("Iris: training fit and holdout")
                 .x_label("petal width (cm)")
                 .y_label("petal length (cm)")
                 .x_limits(.1, 2.5)
                 .y_limits(.5, 9)
                 .legend(
                     {"training", "holdout", "selected fit"},
                     {{150, 150, 150}, {190, 100, 35}, {40, 100, 190}});
  auto check =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .points(test.numeric_column("Petal.Length").values(), pred, "holdout", {40, 100, 190}, 3)
          .line({.5, 7.5}, {.5, 7.5}, "identity", {130, 130, 130})
          .title("Thirty untouched predictions")
          .x_label("observed petal length (cm)")
          .y_label("predicted petal length (cm)")
          .x_limits(.5, 7.5)
          .y_limits(.5, 8.8)
          .legend({"holdout", "identity"}, {{40, 100, 190}, {130, 130, 130}});
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(fit).add(check).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/krr_iris_holdout.svg");
  std::print(
      "Chosen within training rows\n\n{}\n\nRefit diagnostics\n\n{}\n\nUntouched holdout\n\n{}\n",
      cv.candidates.filter([](const auto& r) { return r.get_double("selected") == 1; }).to_md(6),
      m.diagnostics().select({"lambda", "gamma", "df", "training_rmse", "loo_rmse"}).to_md(6),
      m.score(test).to_md(6));
}
```
